2. Max how many columns we can create clustering in bigquery
In BigQuery, you can specify up to 4 clustering columns for a table.
can use clustering on a standalone table (non-partitioned) or combine clustering with partitioning. In a partitioned table, clustering is maintained within each partition.

3. What is Partitioning, Clustering & Sharding in BQ.
Partitioning is like dividing table into smaller partitions for better performance. same as PARTITION BY. Partitioning is per table, not per column.
- DATE/`TIMESTAMP` column (time-unit column-based)
- INTEGER range (range partitioning)
- INGESTION_TIME (automatic partitioning) 
Clustering is like organizing data inside each partition or table based on one or more frequently filtered columns, using sorted blocks.
Sharding is breaking if data into smaller pieces. manually splitting a table into multiple separate tables (not recommended)

