7. Views in BQ
Standard View (Regular View)
A logical SQL query stored in BigQuery. Does not store data physically

Materialized View
Physically stores precomputed and cached results. Automatically refreshes when underlying data changes.
Improves performance and reduces cost for repeated queries. Only supports simple queries (no joins or subqueries).

Authorized View
A specially permissioned view used to restrict data access. Allows users to query data without direct access to base tables. Useful for data masking, sensitive data control.

